Z||000000||ChadMan||10-07-2000||07:51 PM||||I saw a really, really nice Formula at the Valvoline Runoffs (SCCA Nationals) at Mid-Ohio today.  It was white with a beechwood interior, leather seats (Mr. Mike's?), some really cool aftermarket wheels, and was lowered.  The coolest mod:  Wilwood brake calipers - looked like 4-piston!  Kentucky plates.  I didn't have a camera -- D'OH!<P>Anybody know whose car this is?  I had no idea Wilwood made brakes for Fieros.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Rodney||10-08-2000||12:28 PM||||I am interested in this. Anyone have any info?? Did he retain the stock rotors??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||10-08-2000||03:11 PM||||i'm wondering where in ky. the most i see anyone besides my self do to a fiero is some wheels and a window tint, and even thats rare.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||10-08-2000||05:01 PM||||The only other details I can remember about this Formula is that he (she?) had a woodgrain dash kit, a trailer hitch, and the black "beltline" trim around the car was painted white like the rest of the car.  God I wish I had my camera there.  I swear on my grandfather's grave this car had Wilwood calipers - I never would have noticed had I not bent down to take a closer look at his cool wheels.<P>I'm surprised we didn't see this Formula at the FOCOA Nationals.  I can't imagine I guy loving his Fiero enough to do a Wilwood brake conversion, but not going to the FOCOA nationals in his home state!<P>I also saw Keith N.'s yellow 88 Coupe with Quad 4 conversion, a red 88 GT with Michigan plates and no wing, and an 84 or 85 SE with badly faded black paint at Mid-Ohio yesterday.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sleeper||10-08-2000||05:26 PM||||Jesus man don't have a heartattack, go to <A HREF="http://www.wilwood.com" TARGET=_blank>www.wilwood.com</A>  and order one of their catalogs. The calipers you would probably want on your fiero are the Dynalite 2's. I don't really know if they bolt directly on, they might need a big brake kit/bigger rotors.||||reg||12
